    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 1947 UN Partition Plan, proposed by the United Nations Special Committee on Palestine (UNSCOP), divided Palestine into separate Jewish and Arab states, with Jerusalem under international control. Jewish leaders sought a \"state of Israel\" based on the Hebrew Bible, where Zionists had been a smaller minority among Arabs. Meanwhile, Arab leaders and the Palestinian population felt that this plan would divide their land, recognize Jewish sovereignty, and lead to the loss of Palestine as a whole. Many Arab states and some Palestinian leaders alleged that the plan was imposed on the Arab population without their consent, ignored the existing Palestinian Arab presence, and disregarded the country's infrastructure and resources, thereby justifying their refusal to recognize the Jewish state.",
